juno-drivers (0.5.48.2+diamon9) unstable; urgency=low

  * clevo-keyboard-dkms payload bumped to tuxedo-keyboard 4.6.2+diamon3
    (61a47d1): charge_type_store and charge_control_start/end_threshold_store
    now call power_supply_changed() after writing the EC, so upower and KDE
    re-read the threshold instead of serving a cached value (upower kept
    showing 80 while sysfs already held 85). Flexicharger EC errors
    (clevo_has_legacy_flexicharger, clevo_legacy_flexicharger_read,
    clevo_has_cc4_flexicharger) propagate instead of being masked; cc4
    read-modify-write access is serialized by a mutex; the WMI pkgbuf path
    (clevo_wmi_interface_method_call_pkgbuf) returns -EOPNOTSUPP instead of a
    false success; the ACPI object leak on the 0x46 call at init/resume is
    fixed.
  * clevo-keyboard-dkms: postinst reloads udev (when /run/udev/control
    exists) after the diamon8 rm_conffile removes the flexicharger restore
    rule, so the running daemon stops executing the removed rule from its
    cached rules instead of waiting for the next reboot.

 -- DiamonDinoia <marco@localhost>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 10:05:42 -0400

juno-drivers (0.5.48.2+diamon8) unstable; urgency=low

  * clevo-keyboard-dkms: removed the flexicharger restore machinery
    (/etc/clevo-flexicharger.conf, 60-clevo-flexicharger-restore.rules,
    /usr/lib/clevo-keyboard-dkms/flexicharger-restore). Charge control is
    KDE-only: the udev rule re-imposed the conf on every BAT0 add|change
    (10-30 events/s, ~615k helper runs/boot), clobbering KDE Charge Limit
    writes in under a second and hammering the EC with ~2.4e3 store
    transactions/min. Analysis: ../tuxedo-keyboard/juno/analysis/
    2026-09-07-charge/D2-kde-api.md and D4-kde-only-plan.md. Both /etc
    paths shipped as conffiles since diamon6, so a new
    clevo-keyboard-dkms.maintscript rm_conffiles them at 0.5.48.2+diamon8~.
    Payload pin unchanged (c37e4cf / 4.6.2+diamon2).

 -- DiamonDinoia <marco@localhost>  Mon, 07 Sep 2026 18:30:00 -0400

juno-drivers (0.5.48.2+diamon7) unstable; urgency=low

  * juno-drivers-diamon: clevo-keyboard-dkms moves from Recommends to
    Depends. clevo-keyboard-controller (still a Recommends, pulled from
    Juno's repo) hard-Depends on clevo-keyboard; with the driver deb merely
    recommended, apt kept Juno's unpatched clevo-keyboard and dropped the
    patched one, so a fresh default install lost the cc4/0x46 charging fix
    and failed outright wherever Juno's dkms postinst cannot build
    (containers). The hard Depends resolves the controller chain through our
    Provides/Conflicts/Replaces instead.

