juno-drivers (0.5.48+local1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Rebased onto upstream 0.5.48~debian (adds GNOME logout button).
  * Added libhidapi-hidraw0 and libhidapi-libusb0 runtime dependencies (new in
    upstream 0.5.47).
  * Retained the split juno-drivers / juno-drivers-local design.
  * Retained the PPD-aware juno-cpufreq.rules gating (skip the cpufreq udev
    symlink when power-profiles-daemon is present).
  * Kept the local dependency policy; juno-pp remains dropped and was not
    reintroduced by upstream's Depends/Recommends reorganization.
  * Dropped the juno-archive-keyring Depends: diamondinoia-repo-juno carries
    the same source and key, hash-pinned.
  * Dropped the Recommends (gaudible, geoclue-position, juno-wallpaper,
    memtest86+, steam-devices). juno-info stays.
  * postinst runs systemctl offline and guards glib-compile-schemas, so the
    package also configures in a container, which is where CI tests it.

